# Project check contract.
#
# The canonical gate is offline and deterministic: `chaoslab verify` regenerates
# every derived report from the cached Modrinth responses into a scratch root and
# compares the bytes with the committed files and reports/MANIFEST.sha256.
#
# `make check` covers PROJECT_PLAN.md, candidates.txt, pack_manifest.json, the
# mod/ contract (schema, datapack, examples, config), every cached .mrpack plus
# its .mrpack.json sidecar, and every artifact pinned in
# reports/MANIFEST.sha256. That manifest — not the whole reports/ directory — is
# the authoritative list of gated reports. It needs no network access and exits
# non-zero on any mismatch or invalid input.
#
# Deliberately ungated, present under reports/ but never regenerated by the gate:
# the smoke and superseded runs (modpacks.md, modpacks_query_smoke.md,
# modpacks_smoke.md, modpacks_quests.md, modpacks_travelers.md,
# mods_matrix_smoke.md, mods_survey_smoke.md), the gate's own self-report
# (verify.md) and the external log triage (runtime_logs.md). They record past
# runs and must not be cited as current verification; if one becomes load-bearing
# evidence, add it to verify's generator set and re-pin the manifest instead of
# widening this comment.
#
# After an intentional report regeneration, run
# `python3 -m chaoslab verify --update` once to re-pin the manifest, then
# `make check`. `make check-fast` validates only the inputs and is cheap enough
# to run on every edit.
#
# Cache integrity: `verify` tolerates a re-packed .mrpack (it digests the
# declared file paths, download URLs and override names, not the container
# bytes), but it rejects a pack whose .mrpack.json sidecar `bytes` field no
# longer matches the file on disk. When refreshing a cached pack, rewrite its
# sidecar in the same operation; never "fix" a failing cache check by deleting
# the sidecars, and never replace a pack without updating the sidecar.

.PHONY: check check-fast

check:
	python3 -m chaoslab verify

check-fast:
	python3 -m chaoslab verify --inputs-only
